  "simplified": [
    "Main cables use smooth octagonal sections, enlarged from 0.92 to 1.64 m. Each group of suspender wires reads as one 0.96 m rope, repeated every 19.1 to 19.4 m.",
    "The deck follows a segmented crown. Open triangular panels and occasional transverse beams stand in for the full stiffening truss. Sidewalks and curbs share one raised strip per side.",
    "Tower legs use stepped, chamfered sections. Each portal keeps its stepped brackets and a broad central rib. Plate seams, individual cells and rivets are omitted.",
    "The four Fort Point ribs and their posts are retained. Anchorage housings, pylon caps and approach bents use simplified sections. The foundations stop 3 m below mean sea level.",
    "Lights, guardrail pickets, safety netting, road markings, terrain and water are omitted."
  ],
